## Run it

```bash
uv sync --locked                                  # exact dependencies, no resolution
uv run scenario scenario={{ scenario_id }} map={{ map_group }}
```

`--locked` is deliberate: if `uv.lock` and `pyproject.toml` ever disagree, the
command fails instead of quietly resolving something new. That is what makes
this directory reproducible.

The framework's CARLA client is an optional extra and is **not** locked here,
because the client wheel is not published to PyPI. Install it into the same
environment before running against a live server.

## Test it

```bash
uv run pytest
```

The bundled tests load, validate and compile the document. They need no CARLA
server, so they work as a smoke test anywhere.

## Layout

```
{{ package_dir_name }}/
|-- pyproject.toml              # dependencies, pinned exactly
|-- uv.lock                     # the resolved dependency graph (commit this)
|-- .python-version             # {{ python_version }}
|-- conf/
|   `-- scenario/{{ scenario_id }}.yaml   # Hydra config for this scenario
|-- scenario/
|   |-- document.yaml           # the Scenario IR -- edit this
|   `-- manifest.yaml           # what this package was generated from
|-- src/{{ package_name }}/
|   |-- __init__.py             # register() -- the entry point target
|   `-- scenario.py             # binds the document to DeclarativeScenario
`-- tests/
    `-- test_scenario.py
```

